---
exclude_paths:
  # Vendored upstream Flux component set, pinned and copied verbatim. Its
  # formatting is upstream's business, and reformatting it would defeat the
  # point of pinning it.
  - files/gitops_source/cluster-state-static/

skip_list:
  # This repository orders task keys name -> controls -> module -> vars, so the
  # module and its arguments stay one unbroken block and a reader sees whether
  # a task runs before reading what it does. ansible-lint prescribes a
  # different order. See plan/ANSIBLE_STANDARDS.md.
  - key-order[task]

  # Task names are prefixed with the file they live in — `main | Ensure ...` —
  # so a failure names the file to open. That makes the first character
  # lowercase, which this rule reads as a sentence-casing mistake.
  - name[casing]

  # Internal role variables are spelled `_var_`, `_reg_` and `_item_` by their
  # role rather than by the role name alone, so where a value comes from is
  # readable at the point of use. This rule expects the role name first. The
  # role's public parameters — the ones this rule exists to protect — do carry
  # the role prefix. See plan/ANSIBLE_STANDARDS.md.
  - var-naming[no-role-prefix]

  # The naming scheme above makes some expressions unavoidably wide — a task
  # that indexes a registered result by the producing loop's variable cannot be
  # written short. Readability of the name wins over the column limit.
  - yaml[line-length]
  - line-length
